Subject: fix(triage): pass the forge host into the sandbox

An agent running inside the sandbox reaches GitHub through gh, which takes its
host from GH_HOST and, for any host that is not github.com, its credential from
GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN rather than GH_TOKEN. The GitHub overlay passes neither, so
every call the agent makes goes to github.com regardless of where the run is
executing, and on an enterprise install the pre-flight connectivity check fails
before the agent starts.

Both values are already resolved on the host by the time the sandbox env file
is built. Pass them through rather than rederiving them: that file is expanded
before it is copied in, so it cannot carry shell logic to work them out itself.

Passing GH_TOKEN alone is not a partial fix but a wrong one. gh will not read
it on an enterprise host, so the agent authenticates with whatever the
environment already held in GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN - which is the credential the
run was launched with, not the one minted for the agent's role. It looks
identical in the log.

On github.com both expand to empty, which gh treats as unset, so behaviour
there is unchanged.

Scoped to the triage harness, which is the one exercised here. The same overlay
shape appears in the other agent harnesses and would need the same two lines.

Breadboard note: this patches fullsend-ai/agents and is applied to the agents
mirror by deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py. Written to be sent
upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a human-authored
change.

diff --git a/harness/triage.yaml b/harness/triage.yaml
index 889e41c..5e521c6 100644
--- a/harness/triage.yaml
+++ b/harness/triage.yaml
@@ -67,6 +67,14 @@ overlays:
       sandbox:
         ISSUE_URL: "${GITHUB_ISSUE_URL}"
         GH_TOKEN: "${GH_TOKEN}"
+        # gh reads its host from GH_HOST and, for any host that is not
+        # github.com, its credential from GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN rather than
+        # GH_TOKEN. Without both, every call the agent makes inside the
+        # sandbox goes to github.com no matter where the run is executing.
+        # GH_TOKEN alone would leave the agent authenticating as whatever the
+        # environment already held rather than as the minted role.
+        GH_HOST: "${GH_HOST}"
+        GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN: "${GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN}"
         FULLSEND_FORGE: github
   - when: '(has(event.source) && event.source.system == "gitlab") || (!has(event.source) && runtime.forge == "gitlab")'
     providers:
